   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Andrew and Tait,<div><br></div><div>Sorry for the long delay in looking into this. It turns out that the routine for reading those matrix sections from Mplus output was not handling the Fortran-style scientific notation (e.g., 1.225D-03) where the D is similar to the usual e in scientific notation, but explicitly denotes a double-formatted number. Anyhow, it&#39;s a Fortranism that I had seen, but hadn&#39;t thought about in text file parsing. I changed the routine so that any matrix-style output section now supports this D notation.</div><div><br></div><div>I have committed the update to Github, so you can install the development version to get the fix.</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Michael</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Friday, April 17, 2015 at 9:28:07 AM UTC-4, Andrew Schaper wrote:</div></div>"
    ],
